 facts=["Evaluators never block anything, even when they run on live traffic.",
        "**Where you set them:** the portal's Evaluation page (pick a dataset or an agent, then evaluators); the agents playground (on by default, and billed); continuous evaluation on a deployed agent (with a sampling rate); or code: `azure-ai-evaluation`, cloud runs with `builtin.*` evaluators, in CI.",
        "**Three kinds:** maths (F1, BLEU, ROUGE, METEOR, GLEU, String Checker: deterministic, no model); AI-assisted (quality, RAG, agent: an LLM judge on **your** deployment, so you pay its tokens); Microsoft-hosted (safety evaluators, Groundedness Pro: billed as a Foundry service).",
        "**Why not always on:** every evaluator is extra calls per answer and can cost more than the app; many need inputs you may not have (ground truth, context, tool definitions); uncalibrated judges create noise; and they never block. Pick per app, sample live traffic, and keep cheap deterministic rules everywhere.","Evaluators score a single **turn** by default; scoring a whole **conversation** needs data in the messages format.","Combos from Learn: RAG → Retrieval + Groundedness + Relevance + safety; agents → Output Quality + Tool Use Quality + Rubric + safety; translation → BLEU + METEOR + Fluency + Coherence."],
 traps=["\"Continuous evaluation\" sounds live, but it scores answers users have already seen.","The Indirect Attack *evaluator* measures; *Prompt Shields* blocks."],
